  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "pv-resp",
   "title": "Pharmacovigilance Committee — Responsibilities",
   "body": "- Shall meet once in 3 months; responsible for planning, implementing and monitoring the activities of the Pharmacovigilance Programme of India (PvPI).\n- Designated persons are also responsible for sensitising faculty, resident doctors and students in the area of ADRs.\n- To carry out causality assessment of ADRs.\n- To undertake scientific and research activities pertaining to ADRs.\n- To take up activities to strengthen the ongoing National Pharmacovigilance Programme."
  },
